/.yarn/releases/*    binary
/.yarn/plugins/**/*  binary
/.pnp.*              binary linguist-generated

# The JS boundary log's shared byte vectors, pinned byte for byte: SHA256SUMS
# lists each file's SHA-256, libs/jsbound/tests/vectors.rs
# (`sha256sums_cover_every_vector_file`) checks every file against it, and
# codetracer-js-recorder vendors the directory and compares its SHA256SUMS with
# this one byte for byte. Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`,
# which would check out every multi-line `.json` vector and SHA256SUMS itself
# with CRLF line endings, so they would no longer be the bytes their hashes
# were taken of. `-text` turns off line-ending conversion whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says (https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes, "text"); the
# `.bin` vectors carry no NUL byte, so git's binary heuristic would not protect
# them either. The rule lives here, not in a .gitattributes inside the
# directory, because that directory may hold only the files SHA256SUMS lists.
/libs/jsbound/vectors/** -text
/libs/jsbound/vectors/*.bin -diff
